Maintainer: Ethan Bass <ethanbass@gmail.com>
Description: Tools for high-throughput analysis of HPLC-DAD/UV
    chromatographic data. Provides functionality for preprocessing,
    alignment, peak detection, peak model fitting, peak table construction,
    and data visualization. Chromatogram alignment is available via
    parametric time warping (as implemented in 'ptw') or variable penalty
    dynamic time warping (as implemented in 'VPdtw'). Peak detection is
    based on a first-derivative zero-crossing algorithm, and peak shapes
    are fitted using non-linear least squares. Underlying methodologies
    are described in: Wehrens et al. (2015) <doi:10.1007/s11306-014-0683-5>
    for preprocessing and peak table construction; Eilers (2004)
    <doi:10.1021/ac034800e> and Wehrens et al. (2015) 
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btv299> for parametric time warping; Clifford &
    Stone (2012) <doi:10.18637/jss.v047.i08> for variable penalty dynamic time
    warping; Tom O'Haver
    <https://terpconnect.umd.edu/~toh/spectrum/PeakFindingandMeasurement.htm>
    for peak detection; Lan & Jorgenson (2001)
    <doi:10.1016/S0021-9673(01)00594-5> for exponential-Gaussian hybrid
    fitting; and Naish & Hartwell (1988) <doi:10.1007/BF02268168> for
    bi-exponentially modified Gaussian fitting.
